    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class and it's the full suite. The build is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I implemented so `membershipNumber` is assigned as `<customerCode>-M<YY>`:\n\n- **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field (`membership_number` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`AssignMembershipNumber`** (new function class) \u2014 sets `membershipNumber` to `customerCode + \"-M\" + YY`, where `YY = registrationDate.getYear() % 100` zero-padded to two digits (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in after `customerCode` (so both the customer code and the registration-date default are already set) and before `namesakes`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name into the response.\n- **Schema SQL** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added the `membership_number` column so the persisted value survives the create\u2192GET round-trip.\n\nTest suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the sole test class) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
